                        6. Conclusion

In this work, we introduced Repo Navigator, a repositorylevel issue localization agent that departs from existing multi-tool paradigms by leveraging a single, more-capable jump tool for symbol resolution. This unified design faithfully reflects real code execution flow while significantly

chaining. Through tool-integrated GRPO, Repo Navigator learns to reason, invoke tools, and refine its predictions in a

out relying on closed-source teacher models or distillation.

Extensive experiments across SWE-bench-Verified and SWE-bench-Pro demonstrate that Repo Navigator achieves state-of-the-art localization performance. We theoretically analyze the results, confirming that a single powerful tool, jointly optimized with reinforcement learning, can provide 

scoped tools.


---

Our findings highlight the importance of aligning agent tool- References ing with real execution structure, and show that efficient reasoning-tool co-training can unlock substantial gains even for medium-sized open-source models. Future work will 

