## A. Detailed Illustration of Baselines

 Agentless (Xia et al., 2024) is a workflow for issue localization. First, it identifies suspicious files in the 

based on the classes and functions.

 CoSIL (Jiang et al., 2025) is an agent which first 

of modules (class, functions) during the repo-level searching process, and applies context pruning to effectively reduce the searching scope.

Loc Agent (Chen et al., 2025) is almost a fullyautomatic LLM agent besides its planning prompt concatenated into the context at the beginning of the searching process. It builds the whole repository into a direct heterogeneous graph, whose nodes are files, classes, and functions. Additionally, edges are built by dependencies such as imports and invocations. Multiple graph-level searching tools are equipped to the LLM for multi-hop reasoning.

 Repo Searcher (Ma et al., 2025) is an agent 

close-source model (Claude3.7-Sonnet in Repo Seacher) as warmup and reinforcement learning to further enhance the performance.

Ours Compared with all baselines, we are the first fullyautomatic LLM agent, with no fixed workflow and no planetary prompt, and we are the first method trained directly from pretrained open-source LLMs without a close-source teacher model. Lastly, we only integrate a single yet powerful tool to the agent, which reduces compounding error and

narrows the access scope of the agent.

